 I&rsquo;d been wanting to do this version of babka for a while. To start with, I make it with tangzhong, an ultra-quick preparation based on milk and flour that gives buns an incomparable softness. Here the babka has a totally addictive consistency! So this time I&rsquo;m offering you an alternative to chestnut cream, walnuts and cream cheese. The result is not at all too sweet, as the acidity of the cream cheese breaks up the sweetness of the chestnut cream. Sure, it&rsquo;s rich, but absolutely delicious and this babka will be perfect for a weekend snack or brunch! &#13;



 &nbsp; 
 &nbsp; 
&#13;
