content:
  
 @Claire Curt for « Scandalously Decadent », Flammarion 
 



 I propose you a recipe unpublished on the blog, but which I published in my book Scandalously Decadent, published by Flammarion, which you can find in your bookstore! This pie from Florida, USA, is simply magical! The raw cream is liquid, I don&rsquo;t put an egg in it, and yet it congeals in an incredible way, the lemon juice coagulating the sweetened condensed milk and Greek yogurt. The result is a well-balanced pie, fresh, not so sweet thanks to the lime juice and melting in the mouth. It is traditionally made with small limes from the Keys, but I&rsquo;ve never seen them here. You can replace them with classic limes without any problem. A delight, especially with a good lemon whipped cream! 


 
   
 


