I give you here my recipe of Catalan cream after my culinary trip in Barcelona. Very close visually to the crème brûlée (my recipe  HERE ), the consistency is however very different. I suggest a preparation in a water bath, which for me is the only real solution to avoid boiling the cream, to avoid lumps and which guarantees a silky cream ! With its lemon and cinnamon flavour, crema catalana is one of the world&rsquo;s must-have desserts!&nbsp; 
&nbsp; 
&nbsp; 
Recipe for 4 individual Catalan creams: 
&nbsp; 


 500ml of fresh whole milk&nbsp;  
 90g of sugar  
 100g of egg yolk  
 30g of cornstarch  
 the peel of an untreated lemon  
 1 cinnamon stick&nbsp;  
 1/2 teaspoon liquid vanilla extract  
 1 pinch of salt&nbsp;  


&nbsp; 
Instructions: 
 Put the fresh whole milk, half of the sugar (45g), cinnamon, vanilla and untreated lemon peel (without the white part). In the photo, my cinnamon stick broke in half.&nbsp;  
 &nbsp;

