A very soft, tender and tasty cake with a good taste of honey and nuts, that&rsquo;s what I wanted after the change to winter time&#8230; It&rsquo;s so gray that I wanted to crawl under the comforter and feel a cake baking in my oven. Well, it&rsquo;s true that my kitchen has become a real factory for almost 4 years and it smells like cakes every day&#8230;! This one is super simple to make and you can even make it in muffin tins (because it puffs up nicely) or a cake pan. For my part, it is in cake format to cut a nice slice that I enjoyed with my hot latte&#8230;&nbsp; 
&nbsp; 
&nbsp; 

Recipe for 18cm Honey Nut Cake: 
&nbsp; 
 -185g of nuts  
 -120g of soft butter  
 -115g of honey  
 -50g of caster sugar  
 -40g of brown vergeoise  
 -180g of egg  
 -150g of flour  
 -1/2 teaspoon baking powder&nbsp;  
&nbsp; 
Instructions:&nbsp; 
 Preheat your oven to 170°C.  
 Start by coarsely blending 125g (of the 185) of nuts.  

