I am constantly on the hunt for the ultimate cake. And when I find a recipe that works, I&rsquo;ll post it right away! I tried this version during a cooking workshop and the students loved it. I promised them to publish the recipe as soon as possible! It&rsquo;s done with this orange cake: zest and candied peel marinated in Cointreau and chocolate chips. The texture is just the way you like it: a little crunchy on the outside and rich on the inside&#8230;&nbsp; 

&nbsp; 
&nbsp; 

&nbsp; 
Orange and chocolate cake recipe for 6 people: 
&nbsp; 
 -75g of soft butter  
-75g of semi-salted butter  
-150g of powdered sugar  
-the zest of an orange  
-3 large eggs  
-250g of flour type 55  
-8g of baking powder  
-150g candied orange peel in pieces  
-15g of cointreau  
-150g of milk or dark chocolate chunks  
Instructions: 
 Pour the cointreau over the candied orange peels and let marinate while you prepare the dough.&nbsp;

