 Why a churro recipe, when you can often find simple proportions with measuring cups? Because I find it too random. And finally, the proportion of water is important in the recipe: too much water and the churros will swell under the effect of the steam and will end up deformed and very airy, not enough water and the churros will be very hard with an interior like dry breadcrumbs. The ratio I give you here gives you a perfect result: churros that hold together and a soft interior. I don&rsquo;t use eggs, sugar or milk. Just water and flour and the result will please all food lovers (at least, I hope so!).  

