thanks to brigitte riou, a friend of my mom, who got her recipe from her grandmother. a perfect recipe for cat&rsquo;s tongue. a thin, light and very crispy cookie with a good taste of butter! everyone knows this fine cake and i was surprised to discover the best cat&rsquo;s tongue recipe thanks to brigitte. so a big thank you! 



 recipe for cat&rsquo;s tongues: 
   -135g of egg whites   
  -100g of flour   
  -125g of sugar   
  -2 packets of vanilla sugar   
  -125g of&nbsp;butter   
  preheat the oven to 180°c.  
 melt the butter.  








 mix&nbsp;sugar and vanilla sugar.&nbsp;  







 mix butter and sugar to a cream.&nbsp;  







 add flour and mix well.&nbsp;  







 beat the egg whites until stiff, then add them to the previous mixture, lifting well to prevent the whites from falling back.&nbsp;  







 the dough is ready!  







