I took advantage of a&nbsp;trip to Shanghai &nbsp;to take a crash course in dim sum, those little Chinese bites that range from chicken feet to delicately folded and steamed ravioli. So today, the shrimp ravioli. I had already practiced before leaving for the particular folding of these « Har gow » but once&nbsp;in Shanghai I was surprised by the variety of these foldings and that finally it was quite easy. The trick is to have it explained to you. It&rsquo;s true that with this particular course, I had the time to understand well and to repeat myself as many times as necessary until I passed! 
&nbsp; 

&nbsp; 

All the ingredients can be found in Asian grocery stores, especially the wheat starch. 

Recipe for shrimp riavolis (36 pieces): 
&nbsp; 
