Just for the smell of them baking, you have to try these incredible shortbreads. They are very rich in butter, but that&rsquo;s not all! I use fresh lemon peel and candied lemon peel (with sugar), but also cardamom. Since they are relatively low in sugar, the lemon juice glaze is perfect. I had read about this combination of flavors in the American « flavor » magazine and wanted to make my version in my studio. To be made quickly at home, because it is also very easy to make.&nbsp; 

Recipe for about thirty shortbread&nbsp; 
&nbsp; 
&nbsp; 

 85g of sugar  
 225g of soft butter  
 the zest of half a lemon, untreated  
 60g of candied lemon peel  
 350g of flour  
 1/16 teaspoon of yeast (a pinch of knife)  
 12 cardamom pods  
 1/4 teaspoon of salt  

&nbsp; 
&nbsp; 

 200g of powdered sugar  
 45g of lemon juice  

&nbsp; 
&nbsp; 
Pour the sugar and chopped butter into the bowl of your food processor or into a container.&nbsp; 
&nbsp; 


&nb

