This is a recipe I&rsquo;ve been making often since a very good friend of mine from Pau (Christine!) made it for me a few years ago. A delicious duck breast perfectly cooked, with slices of mango cooked in the duck fat. The whole thing is topped with a caramelized sauce with balsamic vinegar, honey and Grand Marnier flambé. A little gem that guests always appreciate! I suggest a method to pre-cook your duck breast before dinner (in the afternoon) and avoid the smell of fat during the meal. The result is fantastic and the duck stays as pink as you like.&nbsp; 



 For once in a recipe, I use a Picard product! I do buy their mangoes, because they are very good, and they are convenient to use. Because it is quite difficult to get nice slices without skin with fresh mangoes.&nbsp;  

Recipe for duck with mango for 4 people: 
   -2 beautiful duck breasts   
  -8 slices of frozen mango (picard!)   
  -2-3 tablespoons of balsamic vinegar   
  -2 teaspoons of honey&nbsp;

