when you think about it, this recipe is&nbsp;completely&nbsp;crazy: it is fatty, there is&nbsp;almost&nbsp;no vitamin, the body stores it directly in our dear fatty capitons&#8230; yes, but it&rsquo;s so good! since i was 12 years old, when i went to the united states for the first time with a family&nbsp;american, i&rsquo;m looking for a recipe that would give me excellent « onion rings », those onion fritters so&nbsp;crispy.&nbsp;i&rsquo;ve eaten a lot of them over the past few years to get a feel for what i like (can you imagine the sacrifice?).&nbsp;&nbsp;i knew what i wanted: doughnuts that stay&nbsp;crispy&nbsp;for a long time. this is the same problem as shrimp fritters (recipe  here ). everything is solved by getting rid of the eternal egg (that&rsquo;s what makes the doughnuts soft after 5 minutes). thanks to my blog, i now have a legitimate excuse to finally make « onion rings » (it&rsquo;s for a good cause) and i have to admit, it&rsquo;s delicious! 
