i just came back from a fabulous culinary trip in greece, on the island of tinos in the cyclades. a trip that i will publish very soon. on the way back i stopped in athens where i ate a delicious dish: kritharoto with shrimps. i set out to make it again in the workshop to give you the recipe. visually, it&rsquo;s a bit complicated to take a picture of, but the dish is just excellent! trust me, especially if you like shrimp. for once in my cooking blog, i&rsquo;m using the little ourzo pasta, or bird tongues, which finally have many names depending on where they come from. it is prepared a bit like a risotto, with a broth full of flavor.&nbsp; 










