with the weather a bit changeable, i&rsquo;m craving something comforting and reassuring again. i can hear the storm rumbling outside as i write the recipe&#8230; but mostly i have a good piece of this delicious cake next to me. 
as you know, what i like most is to experiment in my studio. i suggest this cake that doesn&rsquo;t look like it, but is deliciously moist and tasty. made with banana, coconut and buckwheat flour, it is naturally gluten-free. i love buckwheat, and i&rsquo;m definitely not kicking gluten out of my diet, but this gives those who are intolerant to it one more option. i enjoyed this cake! you can even have it lactose free, as i use coconut cream and almond and coconut powder. the only time i use it is in the butter for caramelizing the bananas and you can easily replace it with margarine. to do whatever your beliefs, because it is very very good!&nbsp; 






recipe for a 24x18cm rectangular or 23cm circular cake: 


   4 bananas   
   30 sucré sweet sucré bernard

