content:

&nbsp; 


&nbsp; 
I was craving a small salad that was ultra fresh and healthy while still being nutritious. That&rsquo;s the case with this coral lentil salad, cooked  al dente , with raisins, pickled red onion and mint. A little rest in the refrigerator and it will be ready to be devoured for a picnic or a buffet on a sunny day!&nbsp; 

&nbsp; 
&nbsp; 
   Recipe for 4 people:&nbsp;  

 500g of coral lentils  
 1 red onion  
 juice of one lemon  
 100g of raisins  
 1 tablespoon dried mint&nbsp;  
 salt pepper  

 Sauce:&nbsp;  

 2 tablespoons of tahini  
 5 tablespoons of olive oil  
 2 tablespoons of vinegar (I took white balsamic vinegar)  
 1 tablespoon of agave syrup or honey  
 2 teaspoons of mustard  
 salt pepper  

Instructions: 
For the lentils, I only cook them&#8230; 5 minutes in boiling water. This is much less than the usual cooking time, but it makes for perfect  al dente  lentils in a salad! 

&nbsp; 

Rinse in cold water

