 After the holidays, I had a jar of tartufata sauce left over, basically mushrooms with truffle oil. It&rsquo;s super rich in taste and it&rsquo;s a delight with lots of things. I suggest this association, rather than a real recipe, with Brillat-Savarin, this very creamy cheese and ham. This gives a perfect result: a crispy croque-monsieur on the outside and soft and melting on the inside, ideal for a quick meal with a good salad! &#13;
&#13;
